P mass**\n- Before: **103**\n- After: **102**\n- Change: **-1**\n\nThe helper adds a binding but removes repeated coordinate-format constants/operations; more importantly, the Rule 2 clarity improvement takes precedence over the small mass reduction.\n\n**Tests:** `pnpm test` passes — **6 passed, 2 todo**."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_07-10-33_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_gpt-5-6-terra/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/game-of-life.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/game-of-life.ts\nPassing tests: 6\nRecent changes: added deterministic x-then-y output sorting after reproduction selection.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/game-of-life.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/game-of-life.ts\nPassing tests: 6\nRecent changes: added deterministic x-then-y output sorting after reproduction selection.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784963593242},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_mQBcklZ4DRn1WDsfe4SwQI0I","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/game-of-life.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_L2rcteZ4Gzbxafoh9S9K2M3w","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/game-of-life.spec.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3IrAs51HHv1OX3CFeR0lFwig","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"package.json"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_T61dAWPfElUThiMiNPYenYin","name":"find","arguments":{"path":".pi","pattern":"**/*refactor*"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"azure/gpt-5.6-terra@swedencentral","usage":{"input":404,"output":143,"cacheRead":5760,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":46,"totalTokens":6307,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784963593262,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-60c8c8dd-318c-4290-b823-a499478169d4","responseModel":"gpt-5.6-terra-2026-07-09"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_mQBcklZ4DRn1WDsfe4SwQI0I","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export type Cell = [number, number];\n\nexport function nextGeneration(currentGeneration: Cell[]): Cell[] {\n  const liveCellKeys = new Set(currentGeneration.map(([x, y]) => `${x},${y}`));\n  const neighborCounts = new Map<string, number>();\n\n  for (const [x, y] of currentGeneration) {\n    for (let dx = -1; dx <= 1; dx += 1) {\n      for (let dy = -1; dy <= 1; dy += 1) {\n        if (dx === 0 && dy === 0) continue;\n        const key = `${x + dx},${y + dy}`;\n        neighborCounts.set(key, (neighborCounts.get(key) ?? 0) + 1);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  return [...neighborCounts]\n    .flatMap(([key, count]) => {\n      const isLiveCell = liveCellKeys.has(key);\n      if ((isLiveCell && (count === 2 || count === 3)) || (!isLiveCell && count === 3)) {\n        return [key.split(\",\").map(Number) as Cell];\n      }\n      return [];\n    })\n    .sort(([firstX, firstY], [secondX, secondY]) => firstX - secondX || firstY - secondY);\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784963594774},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_L2rcteZ4Gzbxafoh9S9K2M3w","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, expect, it } from \"vitest\";\nimport { nextGeneration } from \"./game-of-life.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Game of Life next generation\", () => {\n  it(\"returns [] for an empty sparse grid -- []\", () => {\n    expect(nextGeneration([])).toEqual([]);\n  });\n  it(\"makes a single live cell die -- [(0, 0)] becomes []\", () => {\n    expect(nextGeneration([[0, 0]])).toEqual([]);\n  });\n  it(\"applies underpopulation -- [(0, 1), (1, 1)] becomes []\", () => {\n    expect(nextGeneration([[0, 1], [1, 1]])).toEqual([]);\n  });\n  it(\"keeps the center cell alive with three neighbors -- (1, 1) remains live\", () => {\n    expect(nextGeneration([[0, 0], [1, 0], [2, 0], [1, 1]])).toContainEqual([1, 1]);\n  });\n  it(\"applies overpopulation -- center cell (1, 1) with more than 3 neighbors dies\", () => {\n    const next = nextGeneration([[0, 0], [1, 0], [2, 0], [1, 1], [0, 2], [1, 2], [2, 2]]);\n    expect(next).not.toContainEqual([1, 1]);\n  });\n  it(\"applies reproduction -- [(0, 1), (1, 1), (0, 0)] becomes [(0, 1), (1, 1), (0, 0), (1, 0)]\", () => {\n    expect(nextGeneration([[0, 1], [1, 1], [0, 0]])).toEqual([[0, 0], [0, 1], [1, 0], [1, 1]]);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"evolves the blinker through two generations -- vertical to horizontal and back\");\n  it.todo(\"keeps the block still life unchanged -- [(0, 0), (1, 0), (0, 1), (1, 1)]\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784963594774},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3IrAs51HHv1OX3CFeR0lFwig","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"name\": \"tdd-experiment-run\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"test\": \"vitest run\",\n    \"test:unit:basic\": \"vitest run\",\n    \"test:watch\": \"vitest\",\n    \"test:coverage\": \"vitest run --coverage --coverage.reporter=json-summary\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.3.0\",\n    \"tsx\": \"^4.7.0\",\n    \"vitest\": \"^1.0.0\",\n    \"@vitest/coverage-v8\": \"^1.0.0\",\n    \"eslint\": \"^9.0.0\",\n    \"eslint-plugin-sonarjs\": \"^1.0.0\",\n    \"typescript-eslint\": \"^8.0.0\"\n  },\n  \"pnpm\": {\n    \"onlyBuiltDependencies\": [\"esbuild\"]\n  }\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784963594774},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_T61dAWPfElUThiMiNPYenYin","toolName":"find","content":[{"type":"text","text":"agents/refactor.md"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784963594774},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_tHGRhLejyA8gznwynfBGm9Od","name":"read","arguments":{"path":".pi/agents/refactor.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_yfzuBctgX8DuXhr8JdBo